   "source": [
    "Newer SCBD checklists (`DDS3-10-JUN`) don't embed the score in the label like the legacy report above (`\"Good (3)\"`). Instead each MC item's real number of levels is defined per-item in `form.checklists.<checklist_key>.extra_config.rubric` — only the non-blank `O1..O5` slots are valid for that item (2, 3, 4 or 5 levels). This section:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Maps the assessor's recorded answer (`\"Done\"`, `\"Mostly done\"`, ...) to its `O`-letter via `form.checklists.<checklist_key>.extra_config.options.assessor`.\n",
    "2. Finds which `O1..O5` slots are non-blank for that specific MC in `extra_config.rubric` → that count is `n`.\n",
    "3. Scores the item as a raw rank `0..(n-1)` based on where its O-letter ranks among the active levels — this raw integer (not a percentage) is what's written to the `MCn (/d)` column, where `d = n-1` for that item.\n",
    "4. Separately normalizes that rank to `0–1` so items with different numbers of levels can still be averaged fairly → overall %, plus a per-domain % using the `extra_config.headers` section groupings (Clinical Info Gathering / Diagnosis & Prognosis / Treatment Planning / Presentation). Checklists with no `headers` config (the 4-item AM/PM checklists) roll up under \"Other\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Note:** `options`, `rubric` and `headers` all live *inside* `extra_config` — confirmed against the live data (not as siblings of it, which the original sample looked like but wasn't).\n",
    "\n",
